{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>ובנחה</b> written with a heh corresponding to the four standards and the camp of the Levites. In the verse ויהי בנסוע there are 12 words, just as there are in the verse ולכל היד החזקה, which is the end of the Torah. And in the verse ובנחה there are 7 words, just as there are in the verse בראשית, which is the beginning of the Torah — to say that it is considered a scroll of the Torah in its own right, and it begins with vav and ends with lamed, corresponding to הליכות עולם ל״ה (the ways of the world are 36). Any parashah that contains enough to gather 85 letters, like ויהי בנסוע, saves from fire — therefore ותבער בם אש ה׳ is adjacent to it, to tell you that a parashah containing 85 letters is saved from fire. And therefore the word that amounts to 85 saves from the judgment of Gehenna."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:48.021261991Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}